  "summary": "Land temporal revisions (T3) and ADD_ENUM in Core under the structural builtin version 2, with the successor state-version profile.",
  "why": "Luis ruled R-01 to R-11 (design/temporal/g4/RULINGS.md): a supersession declares TRANSITION or REVISION, names its target, and Core infers nothing; version_referrers extracts who used a version; Core never recomputes. R-07 required route C with route D before main: builtin malleus.core.operations-apply-atomically v2 applies supersession_kind, v1 keeps its bytes and refuses it, new histories bind STRUCTURAL_HISTORY_BUNDLE, and state-version-v2 separates REVISE from SUPERSEDE. ADD_ENUM (2026-09-23 candidate) lets a live history add a new enum under a successor revision policy. Luis: land T3 with ADD_ENUM in one pass.",
